"Converting Between Mixed Units" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138592 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186139375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138592 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138592 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138592 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "89a1c0b6-a897-5db4-bd62-c855d5db6af2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138798 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186135736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138798 #edb/ref 1069 "q-46132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138798 #edb/ref 1071 "At the start of a launch, a space rocket consumes about $150$ kilograms of fuel per second. How much fuel does it consume per minute?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138798 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "caebe8e5-ea81-5ade-8b5b-0cc8c14fd9cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138798 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138799 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186135742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138799 #edb/ref 1069 "q-46322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138799 #edb/ref 1071 "The cheetah is considered the fastest land animal. It can achieve a speed of $120$ kilometers per hour. What is this speed in kilometers per minute?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138799 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e80e844-aeea-5957-8813-6a48149e9acd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186138799 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139375 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186139376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139375 #edb/ref 1061 3049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139375 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "23d7066f-ee02-59e9-ae85-3a1372e71eea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139375 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186139599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139376 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186139377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139376 #edb/ref 1061 3050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139376 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48400771-1498-544e-a6cb-80f32c6689d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139376 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186138442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139377 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186139378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139377 #edb/ref 1061 3053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139377 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16237576-82b8-5b51-891e-bf6a4b793259" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139377 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186138443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139378 #edb/ref 1061 3056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139378 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "484759f2-e1e7-5618-9ef3-12349540dbce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139378 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186138444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139599 #edb/ref 1064 "We can use unit conversions to convert from one set of units to another.\n\nFor instance, the speed of sound is approximately $0.34$ kilometers per second. What is this in meters per second? We can find out using the following two steps.\n\n** Step 1: Create a conversion formula.**\n\nWe are given the units $\\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{\\textrm{s}},$ and we want to convert this into $\\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}.$ To figure out what we need to multiply by, we can set up an equation to help us:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{s}\\cdot\\, \\dfrac{?}{?} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nWe want to replace $\\textrm{km}$ with $\\textrm{m}.$ To get rid of $\\textrm{km},$ we can put $\\textrm{km}$ in the denominator so that it cancels out:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\\dfrac{\\cancel{\\textrm{km}} }{s}\\cdot \\dfrac{?}{\\cancel{ \\textrm{km} } } = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nThen, to introduce $\\textrm{m},$ we can put $\\textrm{m}$ in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\\dfrac{\\cancel{\\textrm{km}} }{s}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{m} }{\\cancel{ \\textrm{km} } } = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}\n$$\n\nSo, our conversion formula is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{s}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm{m} }{\\textrm{km} } = \\dfrac{\\textrm{m}}{\\textrm{s}}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2: Use the conversion formula.**\n\nNow that we have our conversion formula, we need to determine the correct numbers to use, and apply it.\n\n- The speed that we wish to convert is $0.34 \\, \\dfrac{\\textrm{km}}{\\textrm{s}}.$\n\n- There are $1\\,000$ meters per kilometer.\n\nApplying our conversion formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.34\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{s}} & =0.34\\,\\frac{\\text{km}}{\\text{s}}\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{km}} \\\\  & =(0.34\\cdot 1\\,000)\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{km}}}{\\text{s}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{km}}} \\\\  & =340\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{s}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the speed of sound is $340$ meters per second." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139599 #edb/ref 1065 1404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139599 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d1f56c71-9cb3-5a5b-881c-bfbad588ca7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186139599 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
